# NOTES
# 1. Korea's early foreign-built units (Kori 1-4) show the clearest heuristic-flattening error: the source
#    data assigned KEPCO E&C (architect_engineer) and Doosan Heavy Industries (turbine_supplier) uniformly
#    across the ENTIRE Korean fleet, including units built a decade or more before those firms existed in
#    those roles. Kori 1&2 (1978/1983) actually used Gilbert as AE and GEC Turbines (Rugby, UK) for turbines;
#    Kori 3&4 (1985/1986) used Bechtel as AE and Hyundai as constructor (not Westinghouse), still with GEC
#    turbines. This is the single largest confirmed-wrong cluster in this batch (12 WRONG fields, all Kori).
# 2. The "constructor" field for every domestic-era Korean unit (Hanbit 3-6, Hanul 3-6, all Shin-Kori,
#    Shin-Hanul, Shin-Wolsong — 20 units) is the identical string "KEPCO E&C / Hyundai E&C" regardless of
#    site or build era. This is structurally suspicious: KEPCO E&C is the architect-engineer, not a
#    construction contractor, and actual site builders on Korean NPP projects are known to vary (Hyundai
#    E&C, Samsung C&T, Daewoo E&C, POSCO E&C, Doosan E&C depending on unit/round). I could not confirm the
#    correct site-specific contractor for any of these 20 units this session, so all 20 "constructor" fields
#    are marked UNVERIFIABLE rather than CONFIRMED or WRONG — this is a real gap, not a clean pass, and is
#    the most significant residual finding in the batch.
# 3. Wolsong's rpv_manufacturer = "None" is CORRECT, not a placeholder gap: CANDU reactors use a calandria +
#    pressure-tube design with no single reactor pressure vessel. All 4 Wolsong units confirmed HIGH on this
#    field.
# 4. Maanshan's turbine_supplier was recorded as "Westinghouse" but Wikipedia's Maanshan article explicitly
#    states General Electric manufactured the turbines for this Westinghouse-NSSS plant — confirmed WRONG
#    for both units.
# 5. Hanbit 1&2 and Hanul 1&2 (the other two early-foreign-built Korean pairs, analogous to Kori 1-4) could
#    not be sourced this session — the WebSearch tool hit its session-wide budget cap (200/200) partway
#    through research, and available WebFetch-only sources (Wikipedia plant articles, WNA country profile)
#    did not contain unit-level vendor detail for these two plants. All 16 fields for these 4 units are
#    marked UNVERIFIABLE. Given the confirmed pattern at Kori, it is likely their architect_engineer and
#    turbine_supplier values are ALSO wrong (same anachronism), but this should not be assumed without a
#    source — recommend re-running with a fresh WebSearch budget, targeting Hanbit 1&2 and Hanul 1&2
#    specifically (search terms: "Yonggwang 1 2 Westinghouse constructor architect engineer turbine", "Ulchin
#    1 2 Framatome constructor turbine supplier").
# 6. Taiwan (Chinshan, Kuosheng, Maanshan) constructor/turbine/RPV fields for the foreign vendor itself (GE
#    or Westinghouse) were marked CONFIRMED at MED confidence based on standard turnkey-project practice for
#    plants of this type/era, not unit-specific procurement documents — flagging as a softer confirmation
#    than the HIGH-confidence Korea CANDU finding. The architect_engineer field for all 3 Taiwan plants (6
#    units) could not be sourced and is marked UNVERIFIABLE; Taipower's plants are commonly associated with
#    Bechtel or Ebasco as AE but no source consulted this session named a specific firm for these projects.
